<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James Butler, 1st Earl of Ormond</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1305–1338</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">James Butler, 1st Earl of Ormond, was head of the Anglo-Norman Butler family, hereditary butlers of Ireland. In 1328 he was created Earl of Ormond and granted palatine rights over Tipperary, giving the earls their own courts and officials. His descendants ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kilkenny-castle">Kilkenny Castle</a> and were among the most powerful lords in Ireland.</p></div>
